From 355010b285bcaddf4287f6eca1e681cf03784c73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:09:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The fight, shown: third-person camera, the supplied punching
 animation on both men, you in your own look; faster frames

- Defending no longer blurs and darkens the street: the camera steps out of your eyes to a
  third person's view (behind you, to the street side), the supplied rapid-punching animation
  plays for both of you (baked onto the walking man's skeleton, tools/bakeFight.mjs), he is
  thrown onto his back, and the camera comes back into your eyes for the letter.
- You are drawn after the owner's portrait (swept-back hair, beard, black T-shirt) in the manner
  of the supplied Miles Morales model: banded colour, red and violet rims, halftone, off-register
  outlines; dithered in and out with the camera.
- BAM and POW land with the first blow and the uppercut and leave again.
- Performance: adaptive pixel density (max 1.5 desktop), multisampling only below 1.25x,
  shadows every other frame.
- tools/singlefile.mjs: the one-file build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017Yfam9H7FbQFsBx6yJZ8yW
